packages/main/src/core/process-fact-levels.ts:234:  { name: 'host_run', level: 'L2', category: 'managed-provider-execution', owner: 'handlers/host-run + core/managed-host-run', rationale: 'Submits one durable provider CLI execution whose worker, process group, finite absolute deadline, output projection, terminal and receipt outlive the observing caller. The handler mirrors finite-positive-integer timeout/deadline schema constraints and publishes the exact durable runId through progress before foreground attach so a replacement caller can recover without duplicate spawn. For a managed reviewer, the one-shot capability descriptor settles the controller on local write finish (not worker-side descriptor close), then the independent durable claim handshake bounds detached submission without waiting for provider terminal exit. Shared provider admission is mandatory even with usage accounting disabled, and release mutation failures remain observable. Ordinary output/usage remain diagnostic; formal --managedReview derives the immutable story/reviewRun/lane/provider/material tuple but executes the provider only in a sealed detached scratch at the submitted HEAD while the canonical Story worktree remains the durable audit root. Before launch the controller evaluates the four canonical read-only acceptance report projections in that signed root, injects only a bounded path-free status snapshot into the managed-only derived prompt, and seals that exact derived-prompt digest in the immutable run binding; providers must consume the snapshot rather than invoke those readers from scratch, and unavailable is explicit rather than a cwd-gate bypass. Only the provider adapter bounded final-result lane may produce an unimported proposal. Managed Claude alone receives its mode-0600 one-shot prompt below the exact provider cwd in a sealed runId-bound leaf; normal worker cleanup plus terminal reconciliation/expiry repair remove only that exact leaf after a crash, alongside an explicit non-interactive permission mode and a bounded non-secret JSON Schema bound to the exact managed tuple. Only its successful terminal provider-validated structured_output is proposal input, while prose and fenced JSON fail closed. The detached worker FD selector is removed from the provider environment. Ordinary Claude and Codex launch policy/transport remain unchanged.' },
packages/main/src/core/process-fact-levels.ts:235:  { name: 'host_run_status', level: 'L2', category: 'managed-provider-reconciliation', owner: 'handlers/host-run + core/managed-host-run', rationale: 'Bounded status/long-poll reproduces finite nonnegative integer generation/sequence/wait schema constraints including the exact 30000ms maximum, resolves immutable spec.storyId from runId before ownership admission, reads one exact managed run, and may next-touch reconcile explicit cancel/deadline facts into one terminal receipt. The reserved durable absolute_deadline_exceeded cancellation reason always seals timed_out, while ordinary operator cancellation seals cancelled; both retain the same cleanup proof. A granted launch without provider identity stays replacement-unsafe even after worker death; a recorded process-group reap seals the actual TERM, KILL, reaped, and residual facts. Silence, output age, and observer timeout are never terminal predicates.' },
packages/main/src/core/process-fact-levels.ts:236:  { name: 'host_run_cancel', level: 'L2', category: 'managed-provider-reconciliation', owner: 'handlers/host-run + core/managed-host-run', rationale: 'Resolves the exact immutable spec.storyId from runId, idempotently requests cancellation for that run, and performs bounded process-group reconciliation. It never spawns a replacement and reports replacementSafe only after cleanup is proven.' },
packages/main/src/core/process-fact-levels.ts:237:  { name: 'host_run_worker', level: 'L2', category: 'managed-provider-execution', owner: 'handlers/host-run + core/managed-host-run', rationale: 'Internal, help-hidden runtime-continuation worker durably claims and publishes running ownership before reading one-shot prompt capability, establishes a terminal-lock launch-authority fence before provider spawn, owns shared admission/provider supervision and the explicit provider deadline, ignores ordinary Codex progress agent messages while counting only one schema-valid managed proposal envelope from a Codex agent_message or exact standalone raw stdout block, keeps malformed/multiple/oversized envelope attempts fail-closed, discards an optional findings-only diagnostic note before proposal persistence, serializes live-output/snapshot/terminal writes under one authority lock, seals live-output plus result/event/proposal digests into one terminal receipt plus any imported evidence-binding digest, and remains independent of the caller watchdog.' },
