   109	/**
   110	 * One late-error guard per physical stream. A capped write can still emit EPIPE
   111	 * after its foreground command returns; keeping the per-run listener would grow
   112	 * without bound when a stream never settles. This shared guard is reference
   113	 * counted by pending writes, so it contains that late event while retaining at
   114	 * most one listener for any stream and disappears once the final write settles.
   115	 */
